<h1 id="wo-04-reliable-ingestion-bounded-health-checks-comment-counts-and-program-alerts">WO-04 — Reliable ingestion, bounded health checks, comment counts and program alerts</h1>
<h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
<ul><li>Findings <strong>R09, R11, R12 and R13 remain OPEN</strong>. <code>9fae324</code> is the original review/planning baseline; authorized implementation resumed at <code>c304e85</code>. This work order retains the original task specification, with current execution tracked separately; it is not closure evidence.</li><li>Sixteen atomic tasks, seven Evidence Wave sections, four contract rows, explicit write sets, independent review and QA remain mandatory. Local source/test implementation and synthetic/demo verification are authorized and have run; production deployment, live migration and real sending remain unauthorized.</li><li>Preserve existing Node22/ESM, Firestore roots, domain identities, authorization and durable delivery semantics. No new dependency by default; no exactly-once FCM claim.</li><li><strong>Current scoped implementation:</strong> B15 native 125/125 has independent INTERIM HANDOFF / LOCAL_GREEN approval. B16 T10 is integrated with independent source review, focused 106/106 and full Functions 413/413 GREEN; the canonical helper attachment changes only four export keywords. T11 tooling is in progress; initial 26 preview/import setup guards are not migration/executor acceptance. Native T12 query/index/Rules/carry/stamp, migration/rollback, original 17 identity, final integration/full Flutter/browser/physical-device and independent acceptance gates remain required. All findings remain OPEN; production operations are separately unauthorized.</li><li>Highest risks: changed RSS identity causing duplicates, stale comment recount overwriting newer counts, and notification key migration resending acknowledged/unknown deliveries. Each has explicit bounded migration/rollback controls.</li></ul>
<h2 id="document-information">Document information</h2>
<ul><li>Original planning date: 2026-10-25; authorized continuation: 2026-10-26. Owner: Delivery Lead. Scope: <code>hudhud_fm</code> only.</li><li>Inputs: [technical review](tech-review.md), [content automation](../../docs/contracts/content-automation-contract.md), [station content](../../docs/contracts/station-content-contract.md), [data contract](../../docs/contracts/firebase-data-contract.md), [security](../../docs/contracts/security-privacy-contract.md).</li><li>Existing architecture is retained. No invented PRD or pre-existing new API/module is assumed. <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong> labels below identify files proposed by the original plan. Current presence is recorded in waves.json.fileInventory; an authored or partially authored file is not verified task completion.</li></ul>
<h2 id="0-original-review-preflight-historical-evidence">0. Original review preflight — historical evidence</h2>
<p>The following observations and line references describe the original <code>9fae324</code> review baseline, not the current implementation. B15 / 04-T09 is now in progress; the master execution plan records the current cutpoint and execution-progress.md holds subsequent evidence. Full nonempty reconciliation/restore and the four producer fixes remain unfinished; all findings remain OPEN.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Fact</th><th>Evidence and implication</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Original review baseline</td><td><code>9fae324</code>; this table preserves the planning-era observations. Authorized source/test execution resumed later at <code>c304e85</code></td></tr><tr><td>R09</td><td>[rss-ingestion.js:69](../../functions/lib/rss-ingestion.js:69) copies enclosure attributes without entity decoding; [line196](../../functions/lib/rss-ingestion.js:196) publishes the payload; deterministicEpisodeId/contentIdentity/importKeys/counters/audit must remain coherent</td></tr><tr><td>R11</td><td>[stream-health.js:180](../../functions/lib/stream-health.js:180) scans all stations sequentially; primary+backup can cost16 seconds; [index.js:787](../../functions/index.js:787) has300-second timeout and Dev-before-Official order</td></tr><tr><td>R12</td><td>[comment-moderation.js:170](../../functions/lib/comment-moderation.js:170) updates only comment; [admin-report-review.js:58](../../functions/lib/admin-report-review.js:58) separately decrements; [index.js:644](../../functions/index.js:644) separately counts then overwrites, exposing a race</td></tr><tr><td>R13</td><td>[program-notifications.js:45](../../functions/lib/program-notifications.js:45) ignores schedule offset; line115 uses global Aden time, line133 keys <code>[programId,YemenDate]</code>, line142 revalidates likewise, line164 writes compatibility stamp</td></tr><tr><td>Contract disagreement</td><td>Content contract line37 makes offset explicit and admin validator accepts−720..840; automation §3/durable amendment explicitly use YemenDate and Yemen schedule. Do not silently choose one</td></tr><tr><td>Existing repair precedent</td><td><code>tool/backfill_content_identities.mjs</code> and <code>tool/test/backfill_content_identities.test.mjs</code>: explicit project/root/parent, dry-run, reviewed report, backup, bounds and preconditions; inspect and reuse safe pure patterns, never run or copy destructive behavior blindly</td></tr><tr><td>Harness gap</td><td><code>tool/run-admin-emulator-tests.mjs:35</code> exports only four admin callables; actual comment event handlers are not registered. Merely enabling four PL03 tests would not prove the worker ran</td></tr><tr><td>Existing regression</td><td><code>web_admin/test/pl03-moderation.emulator.test.ts</code> contains new-comment and corrected-counter control cases for both roots; all four must execute, with new-comment evidence independent of manual count seeding</td></tr><tr><td>Tools/CI</td><td>Existing Functions built-in tests/lint, root Rules/admin/editorial/account-deletion/subscriptions emulator scripts; Node22 required. <code>.github/workflows</code> absent in earlier preflight; external CI unknown</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 id="1-design-impact-and-operational-boundaries">1. Design, impact and operational boundaries</h2>
<h3 id="1-1-r09-decode-safely-without-changing-historical-identity">1.1 R09 — decode safely without changing historical identity</h3>
<p>Decode the five predefined XML entities and valid decimal/hex numeric character references in attributes/text <strong>before URL validation and identity calculation</strong>. Reject invalid scalar values/malformed input according to explicit parser policy. No DTD expansion, external entity resolution or new network requests. Prefer a small tested helper in the existing module; add a parser dependency only if correctness cannot be achieved safely and after revising the impact plan.</p>
<p>Existing GUID-less feeds used raw URL text for fallback identity. Corrected decoding therefore must resolve both raw/normalized identity aliases against existing episodes/importKeys before creating anything. Preserve existing episode document IDs, counters, publication flags and audit history; reserve owned aliases to the same ID transactionally. Conflicting aliases stop for review; never merge distinct episodes automatically. Already-bad URLs get a separate reviewed bounded repair, not a broad reimport. Repair must not create/delete episodes, toggle publication, increment parent counts, or emit real publication notifications.</p>
<h3 id="1-2-r11-bounded-fair-progress">1.2 R11 — bounded fair progress</h3>
<p>Preserve sequential station probing and the shared maximum of four outbound fetches per instance; do not bypass <code>public-fetch.js</code> or its8-second deadline. <strong>Proposed budget:</strong>100 seconds per root, at least40 seconds reserved for flushing/cleanup within the existing300-second invocation limit. Before starting a primary+backup pair, require at least16 seconds plus a measured flush margin. If a future timeout changes, derive budget from the same constants.</p>
<p>Persist a private per-root cursor, lease/generation and last completed station ID. <strong>Proposed path:</strong> <code>{root}/streamHealthJobs/checkpoints/active</code>; clients of every role cannot read/write it. Stable document-ID paging must progress for &gt;100 stations and survive station deletion; skip missing records without recreating them. Concurrent invocations cannot both advance/overwrite progress. Keep zero writes to stable station documents under the existing heartbeat policy; checkpoint writes are a separately documented bounded operational exception, not disguised as zero total writes. Inject a clock/probe for deterministic budget tests.</p>
<h3 id="1-3-r12-one-count-authority">1.3 R12 — one count authority</h3>
<p><strong>Proposed module:</strong> <code>functions/lib/comment-counts.js</code>; <strong>proposed private ledger:</strong> <code>{root}/commentCountContributions/episodes/{episodeId}/contributions/{commentId}</code>. Store only contribution/revision/state needed for correctness, no comment body/name/email. No client role may read/write the ledger or directly change counters.</p>
<p>One transaction protocol reads the current comment, episode and prior contribution before writes, calculates the delta between desired/current published contribution and ledger, and updates count/ledger atomically. Event retries/out-of-order events recompute from fresh current state instead of trusting event snapshots. Manual moderation passes its authorized intended transition through the same authority in the same transaction. Account deletion uses the same protocol when removing comments; remove the competing standalone decrement/recount-overwrite path. Never recreate a deleted episode/comment. Define deleted ledger cleanup and delayed-event handling in T01; active contributions cannot expire arbitrarily.</p>
<p>Backfill must initialize ledger and count consistently under a scoped write-quiescence window or a tested revision barrier. A plain aggregate count followed by overwrite is not sufficient. <strong>Proposed limit:</strong>25 items per invocation, explicit episode/root, resumable checkpoint, private before-images and conditional rollback of ledger/counter only—never restore deleted comments or overwrite current moderation. Large episodes require bounded pages plus a final revision-checked activation; no partial active baseline.</p>
<h3 id="1-4-r13-policy-decision-and-delivery-preserving-cutover">1.4 R13 — policy decision and delivery-preserving cutover</h3>
<p>Preferred approved semantics: eligibility weekday/minute/local date and operation key use each schedule's accepted UTC offset. Revalidate the schedule immediately before starting send; a concurrent schedule edit must not mutate an already-bound intent. Retain claim/start/finish, pending/failed/sent/unknown behavior; <strong>unknown never auto-retries</strong>.</p>
<p>Pause old/new workers during the key/date cutover, select a documented cutover day/window, and map old Yemen-date receipts to new local occurrences conservatively. Existing terminal sent/unknown receipts suppress duplicates, including ambiguous cross-midnight overlap. Do not delete receipts or reset lastNotifiedDate to force sends. Where mapping is ambiguous, suppress and require operator review; skipped historical delivery is safer than unauthorized repeat delivery. Rollback pauses workers and preserves both old/new receipt evidence; it does not blindly restore the old key scheme.</p>
<h3 id="1-5-blast-radius">1.5 Blast radius</h3>
<p>High: shared entry point, private state, counters, delivery identity, contracts, maintenance tools and emulator harness. All writes are enumerated below; no new packages or lockfiles planned. Any necessary index update is additive and reviewed by the shared integration owner after WO-03. Production work remains separately authorized; local implementation and synthetic/demo rehearsal do not grant production authority.</p>
<h2 id="2-atomic-tasks">2. Atomic tasks</h2>
<p>Commands are planned <strong>red then green</strong> at the specified cwd. New test files must first be created with executable business assertions; a missing module/file, compilation/environment failure, zero tests or a skip is not valid red evidence. Existing default-deny security assertions may already PASS: retain them as mandatory GREEN guards and never weaken authorization to manufacture RED. Pure test seams may precede the red assertion but must not implement the fix covertly.</p>
<h3 id="04-t01-resolve-policy-and-approve-state-contracts">04-T01 — Resolve policy and approve state contracts</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Data Architect/Delivery Lead. Depends on approved C01/C03 contract-file handoffs before shared edits, not whole WO-01/WO-03 acceptance. B01 emits independently approved C04-RSS/HEALTH/COUNTS/TIMEZONE milestones; T01 remains incomplete until all its outputs are approved. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>docs/decisions/0006-background-consistency-and-schedule-timezones.md</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>docs/contracts/content-automation-contract.md</code>; <code>docs/contracts/station-content-contract.md</code>; <code>docs/contracts/firebase-data-contract.md</code>.</li><li>Decide per-schedule vs fixed-Yemen policy, key/stamp migration, comment-ledger ownership, backfill barrier and health checkpoint exception/budgets. Align descriptions of initial comment status with current behavior; do not silently introduce pending moderation UX.</li><li>Acceptance: independent policy signoff; public/private schema and cutover states explicit; no R13 implementation before decision; operator can distinguish eligibility, send acknowledgement and device receipt.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t02-xml-decoding-and-backward-compatible-ingestion-identity">04-T02 — XML decoding and backward-compatible ingestion identity</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Backend RSS. Depends on approved C04-RSS from T01 and B02 station/relationship handoff, not full T01 or WO closure. Complexity: medium/high.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/lib/rss-ingestion.js</code>; <code>functions/test/rss-ingestion.test.js</code>; <code>functions/lib/admin-content-relations.js</code>; <code>functions/test/admin-content.test.js</code>.</li><li>Implement entity decoding and safe validation; resolve historical/raw and normalized aliases without replacing existing episode IDs; use existing reservation transaction pattern.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/rss-ingestion.test.js test/admin-content.test.js</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: <code>&amp;amp;</code>, predefined/numeric entities and signed query URLs work; DTD/external entity never fetched; malformed entities rejected predictably; GUID and GUID-less reimport creates zero duplicates and preserves counters/audit/publication state.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t03-preview-and-repair-existing-malformed-rss-urls">04-T03 — Preview and repair existing malformed RSS URLs</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Data Tools. Depends on T02. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>tool/repair_rss_urls.mjs</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>tool/test/repair_rss_urls.test.mjs</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>docs/operations/background-consistency-migrations.md</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>.</li><li>Read existing identity-backfill tool/tests for safe patterns; proposed repair defaults dry-run, one explicit root/program, manifest of raw/normalized identities and owned aliases, durable private backup before transaction.</li><li>Red/green, cwd root: <code>node --test tool/test/repair_rss_urls.test.mjs tool/test/backfill_content_identities.test.mjs</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: same episode ID before/after, zero new/deleted episodes, unchanged parent count/publication, alias conflicts fail closed, changed source skipped, resume idempotent, no real notification; rollback restores only owned fields conditionally and preserves alias safety.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t04-fair-bounded-stream-health-scanning">04-T04 — Fair bounded stream-health scanning</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Backend Health. Depends on approved C04-HEALTH from T01, not full T01 or unrelated timezone approval. Complexity: medium.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/lib/stream-health.js</code>; <code>functions/test/stream-health.test.js</code>.</li><li>Introduce injected clock/budget and bounded document-ID pages; stop before a pair would exhaust reserve; preserve sequential probe, backup logic, heartbeat and no raw URL logs.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/stream-health.test.js test/public-fetch.test.js</code>.</li><li>Acceptance:19 dual8-second timeout fixtures cannot starve the second root; &gt;100 stations complete across finite invocations; stable station fields remain zero-write except documented heartbeat; global outbound cap unchanged.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t05-persist-health-leases-cursors-and-integrate-scheduler">04-T05 — Persist health leases/cursors and integrate scheduler</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Backend Health; Integration Owner lands entry-point edits. Depends on T04 and WO-01→WO-03 entry-point handoff. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/lib/stream-health-progress.js</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>functions/test/stream-health-progress.test.js</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>functions/lib/stream-health.js</code>; <code>functions/index.js</code>.</li><li>Implement private per-root leased cursor; make scheduler give both roots their fair bounded budget; deterministic replay/expired-lease recovery, missing-station skip, checkpoint after successful unit.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/stream-health-progress.test.js test/stream-health.test.js</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: two workers cannot lose/regress cursor; timeout/resume advances; deleted cursor station does not block progress; checkpoint write count bounded and distinguished from station writes. Rollback pauses worker, never blindly erases cursor/lease.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t06-single-idempotent-comment-count-authority">04-T06 — Single idempotent comment-count authority</h3>
