<h3 id="04-t16-later-authorized-rollout-and-finding-closure">04-T16 — Later authorized rollout and finding closure</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Operations Lead. Depends on T15 and explicit applicable authorization. Complexity: high.</li><li>File write set: operational document and WO-04 validation report only; environment mutation restricted to approved manifests.</li><li>Quiesce incompatible workers, deploy compatible reviewed versions, execute one root/operation at a time, verify counts/identities/cursors/receipts and independent QA evidence. Keep uncertain delivery suppressed.</li><li>Acceptance: R09/R11/R12/R13 close individually only when their source and scoped operational criteria are proven. Otherwise retain OPEN or documented residual scope; never claim migration success from a code-only test.</li></ul>
<h2 id="3-pre-execution-checklist-and-migration-safeguards">3. Pre-execution checklist and migration safeguards</h2>
<ul><li>Recheck current commit, user edits, AGENTS, contracts and worker definitions; no dispatch on stale evidence.</li><li>Approve R13 policy/ADR and count-ledger baseline/cleanup rules before code. No silent change from YemenDate.</li><li>Compute write-set union and authorize high-impact implementation according to current user authorization. This document alone grants none.</li><li>Every migration proposed above requires explicit project/one root/scope, dry-run default, deterministic reviewed manifest with schema/version/hash and expected source fingerprint, durable private backup verified before mutation, batches of at most25 transactions/concurrency1 by default, resumable lease/checkpoint and conditional restore.</li><li>Backups live outside Git and <code>.boss</code>, contain minimum necessary restricted data, have least-privilege encrypted storage and defined retention. Reports contain counts/status/hashes only, no URLs/tokens/comment content/email.</li><li>Wrong project/root, missing backup, source change, ownership conflict, unknown schema or lost lease stops mutation. No broad delete/update or automatic merge of conflicting identities.</li><li>RSS rollback cannot create/delete/re-publish episodes; count rollback cannot restore comments or stale moderation; notification rollback cannot reset sent/unknown receipts or resend. Health rollback pauses worker and preserves cursor evidence.</li><li>All rollback tooling must preserve WO-01 privacy changes: never restore private station fields to public documents or email to listener profiles from older backups.</li><li>Retain existing authentication, deletion barriers, delivery privacy and public-fetch SSRF/deadline protections. No real Gemini/Telegram/email/FCM as an implicit verification step.</li></ul>
<h2 id="4-dependency-graph-and-evidence-waves">4. Dependency graph and Evidence Waves</h2>
<h3 id="4-0-optimized-dispatch-authority-retain-atomic-tasks-reduce-handoffs">4.0 Optimized dispatch authority — retain atomic tasks, reduce handoffs</h3>
<p>The optimized [master execution plan](execution-plan.md) and [runtime waves](waves.json) own dispatch batching and scheduling. Atomic task IDs, write sets, acceptance criteria, security controls, regressions, migration limits and independent-review gates in this document remain mandatory traceability units; they are <strong>not</strong> instructions to spawn an agent per task. A batch owner retains context across its included tasks and executes their true prerequisites locally. No finding is CLOSED by batching or by an interim patch handoff.</p>
<p>**Every repeated path has exactly one content owner in <code>waves.json.sharedFileOwners</code>.** The original33-path base contained22 I assignments and11 component assignments. All are retained; the current registry has76 unique paths (I: 62, BE: 4, FL: 7, DT: 3), including explicitly approved additive attachments. I retains <code>functions/index.js</code>, Rules/Rules tests, cross-batch relationship modules, the emulator harness, shared contracts/operational documents and shared admin paths according to that exact registry. Specialists prepare patches for I-owned paths without competing working-tree writes. For delegated intra-batch paths, the same component owner writes across its atomic steps without an intermediate I handoff. I integrates the reviewed batch commit without independent content edits; conflicts return to the designated content owner. This ownership refinement changes neither task scope nor acceptance criteria and never permits concurrent writers.</p>
<p>Code/contract handoff is an INTERIM availability event, not WO closure, QA acceptance or a passed Evidence Wave. Co-located count/worker integration and cross-component test work is completed before final acceptance, and all17 previously skipped admin emulator checks must actually run and pass after the real handler is registered. Independent reviewer and QA approvals remain after integrated GREEN, on the exact candidate commit. Manual policy, device, rehearsal and production checkpoints are separate from executable code-wave RED/GREEN; never fabricate RED for an already-correct deny rule.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Legacy section label</th><th>Runtime alias / checkpoint</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>W1 T01</td><td>Manual policy/ADR gate; not an executable RED/GREEN wave</td></tr><tr><td>W2 T02–T03</td><td><code>W04-W2</code></td></tr><tr><td>W3 T04–T05</td><td><code>W04-W3</code></td></tr><tr><td>W4 T06–T09</td><td><code>W04-W4</code></td></tr><tr><td>W5 T10–T11</td><td><code>W04-W5</code></td></tr><tr><td>W6 T12–T15</td><td>Executable integration/authorization portion: <code>W04-W6-CODE</code>; independent review and operational rehearsal remain separate manual checkpoints</td></tr><tr><td>W7 T16</td><td>Separately authorized production checkpoint; not executable code-wave RED</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><code>W04-W6-CODE</code> retains pre-existing private-path denial as baseline/guard GREEN. It is a <strong>guard-only verification wave</strong>, expected to PASS at baseline and after integration; no separate defect RED is required for that wave. Intentional business RED remains in the authored count/real-worker regression of <code>W04-W4</code> and timing/receipt regression of <code>W04-W5</code>, not in a sabotaged permission rule. The runtime artifact distinguishes those defect assertions from invariant guards.</p>
<p>In this WO, BE retains <code>functions/lib/stream-health.js</code> throughout B14 (04-T04/04-T05), preserving one worker context without an intermediate I content-edit handoff. <code>functions/index.js</code> and cross-batch/control files remain I-owned; I integrates the reviewed health commit without independently rewriting its content.</p>
<h3 id="4-0a-exact-optimized-batch-mapping">4.0a Exact optimized batch mapping</h3>
<p>These are the local rows of the master's <strong>16 execution batches</strong>. All <strong>65 atomic IDs</strong> remain:54 implementation/test/contract tasks grouped into batches and11 independent/manual tasks. No atomic acceptance criterion, regression, migration safeguard or scope is removed. Batch worker labels identify retained context; exact content ownership comes from <code>waves.json.sharedFileOwners</code>. I remains the sole content writer only for I-owned paths, while delegated intra-batch paths remain with their component owner. One worker may carry several tasks to completion without a new agent dispatch per ID.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Batch</th><th>Atomic IDs from this WO</th><th>Retained worker</th><th>Batch prerequisites</th><th>Approved contract milestone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>B01</td><td>04-T01</td><td>I</td><td>None</td><td>Produces the four scoped C04 milestones</td></tr><tr><td>B13</td><td>04-T02, 04-T03</td><td>BE</td><td>B02</td><td>C04-RSS</td></tr><tr><td>B14</td><td>04-T04, 04-T05</td><td>BE</td><td>B11</td><td>C04-HEALTH</td></tr><tr><td>B15</td><td>04-T06, 04-T07, 04-T08, 04-T09</td><td>BE+QA</td><td>B06, B09, B11, B12, B13, B14</td><td>C04-COUNTS</td></tr><tr><td>B16</td><td>04-T10, 04-T11, 04-T12</td><td>BE</td><td>B07, B08, B15</td><td>C04-TIMEZONE</td></tr></tbody></table>
<table><thead><tr><th>Manual checkpoint</th><th>Atomic IDs</th><th>Treatment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>G-Q4</td><td>04-T13</td><td>Separate independent/manual checkpoint; preserve the task prerequisites and evidence</td></tr><tr><td>G-R4</td><td>04-T14</td><td>Separate independent/manual checkpoint; preserve the task prerequisites and evidence</td></tr><tr><td>G-O4-READY</td><td>04-T15</td><td>Separate independent/manual checkpoint; preserve the task prerequisites and evidence</td></tr><tr><td>O-4</td><td>04-T16</td><td>Separate independent/manual checkpoint; preserve the task prerequisites and evidence</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>B01 emits separately reviewed <code>C01</code>, <code>C03</code>, <code>C04-RSS</code>, <code>C04-HEALTH</code>, <code>C04-COUNTS</code> and <code>C04-TIMEZONE</code>. Within B01, I applies01-T01→03-T01→04-T01 shared-contract edits serially. Each downstream batch needs only its named approved output, not full B01 or whole-WO closure. The atomic contract task itself remains incomplete until <strong>all its own outputs</strong> are approved. An unresolved R13 decision blocks <code>C04-TIMEZONE</code>/B16 only; it does not block approved unrelated privacy, playback, query, RSS, health or count work.</p>
<p><strong>B15's shared session removes closure cycles:</strong>04-T06 count work and03-T16 regression scaffolding may proceed on disjoint paths; I applies03-T16 harness scaffolding before04-T08, and04-T07 must precede04-T08. The actual worker integration04-T08 precedes04-T09. Independent01-T14 QA runs after B06 privacy work and the required worker integration. Full03-T16 and01-T14 acceptance are <strong>end-B15 results</strong>, never prerequisites requiring completion before04-T08. All17 previously skipped admin emulator identities must run and pass with the actual worker; corrected-counter controls cannot replace new-comment journeys.</p>
<p><code>LOCAL_GREEN</code> means a scoped contract/source patch is ready for its dependent task. It does <strong>not</strong> mean a spanning runtime wave is <code>VERIFIED</code>, the WO is CLOSED, or independent QA/review has passed. In particular <code>W01-W2</code> full admin integration and <code>W03-C</code> full GREEN wait for B15. The original task dependencies still express data and source prerequisites; same-batch prerequisites are local milestones, not forced agent/WO handoffs. Only the explicit replacements in this addendum change their scheduling interpretation.</p>
<p>Parallel execution additionally requires disjoint writable source paths, approved contracts, distinct available workers, and no shared emulator ports/demo state/harness/config/build output. Shared emulator verification uses one exclusive runtime lock; Flutter/build and web output locks follow the master. Installed Boss runtime argv normalization is not claimed to enforce custom batch/lock metadata automatically; the coordinator checks it before dispatch.</p>
<h3 id="4-1-shared-file-ownership-and-safe-parallel-work">4.1 Shared-file ownership and safe parallel work</h3>
<p>Only the relevant named approved T01 milestone gates each branch; pending C04-TIMEZONE does not block C04-RSS/HEALTH/COUNTS. RSS T02→T03; health T04→T05; counts T06→T07→T08→T09; notifications T10→T11. T07 waits T05 because both modify <code>index.js</code>; T12 waits private schema branches and T08 fixture ownership; T13→T14→T15→T16 closes integration. T03→T09→T11 operational-document edits are serial even when module work is parallel.</p>
<p>After their named approved contract milestones and master batch prerequisites, disjoint module tasks T02, T04, T06 and T10 may run alongside disjoint work in other WOs. T05 cannot run concurrently with T04 because both write stream-health; T07 waits all prior shared index ownership. No overlap is permitted merely because tasks are in different Waves.</p>
<p><strong>Handoff is not final acceptance:</strong> WO-04 waits only for WO-01/WO-03 approved contract and shared-source-file handoffs, not their full work-order closure. These are INTERIM handoffs with scoped checks; they do not mark an unfinished QA task or Evidence Wave complete. WO-03 final acceptance needs the actual PL03 worker delivered by04-T08, so requiring WO-03 closure before04-T08 would create a forbidden cycle. Likewise, WO-01 integration QA may wait for this worker; WO-01 need not be globally CLOSED before WO-03 starts disjoint authorized work. After integration, rerun the complete required suite—including all17 previously skipped admin emulator checks—before closing affected QA/Waves/findings.</p>
<p>Central integration order: <code>functions/index.js</code> <strong>WO-01→WO-03→WO-04</strong>; Rules/tests and shared contracts use the same reviewed handoff order where touched; <code>firestore.indexes.json</code> <strong>WO-03→WO-04</strong>, additive only if necessary. <code>admin-app.tsx</code>/Excel remain owned by WO-01→WO-03 and are not WO-04 write sets. The emulator harness has one owner, T08; later QA is read-only unless defects return to T08. Rebase and revalidate after each shared handoff.</p>
<h3 id="4-2-evidence-waves">4.2 Evidence Waves</h3>
