<h3 id="5-2-existing-files-and-serialization">5.2 Existing files and serialization</h3>
<p>Task write sets and their approved registered attachments are authoritative. The original estimate was at most5 paths per task; the explicitly approved B15 fixture/producer attachments below supersede that estimate without changing task IDs or permitting unowned writes. Shared index T05→T07; health T04→T05; operational document T03→T09→T11→T15→T16; validation T13→T14→T15→T16. Rules/index integration occurs after WO-01/WO-03. Existing <code>tool/backfill_content_identities.mjs</code> is a read-only reference unless separately justified and planned; no destructive reuse is assumed.</p>
<h3 id="5-3-verification-scope">5.3 Verification scope</h3>
<p>Node22 Functions unit/lint; existing real emulator scripts and proposed tool tests; tests must identify actual candidate commit and distinguish mocks, emulator worker execution and production evidence. No dependency audit claim, build success, device acceptance, migration execution or production sending is inferred from this plan.</p>
<h2 id="6-standards-and-closure">6. Standards and closure</h2>
<p>Preserve current architecture and error/privacy conventions. Bound queries, retries, scan deadlines and state retention; use transaction reads before writes. Never log raw stream URLs, tokens, account data or comment content. Required QA/reviewer independence is a gate, not self-approval by implementers. Findings remain OPEN until the corresponding fix and authorized operational scope meet their measurable acceptance criteria.</p>
<h2 id="change-log">Change log</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Date</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1.0</td><td>2026-10-25</td><td>English planning-only document; current-source revalidation; no source/tests/deployments/migrations executed</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 id="approved-implementation-amendments-2026-10-26">Approved implementation amendments — 2026-10-26</h2>
<p>The user authorized the complete existing execution plan, with routine in-scope failure repair/retry. Alert eligibility, local date and occurrence identity honor each accepted schedule UTC offset. Independent C04 contracts remain required before source work; no production rollout or receipt migration is authorized.</p>
<p>04-T10 additionally includes the existing <code>functions/lib/notification-delivery.js</code>, exclusively owned by I. Source inspection shows that revalidating a program before a separate delivery-start transaction leaves a schedule-edit race. Reuse the existing delivery protocol with an optional transaction preparation/validation hook, preserving the default behavior of other senders. Current program/station eligibility and bound schedule fingerprint must be read and checked in the same transaction that moves the receipt to sending, with all reads before writes. No duplicate start protocol or new dependency is introduced. This additive path/lock is registered in B16 and W04-W5 before dispatch. Preserve sent/unknown suppression and all existing claim/start/finish contracts.</p>
<p>R12 scope refinement: the ADR0006 C04-COUNTS enforcement amendment and current manifest register all additional guarded producer/test paths within04-T06/07/09. The root freeze includes episode identities, all owned comment/status writers, count-reset maintenance producers and complete ID/createTime inventory verification. The new maintenance helper is dependency-free for standalone seed use. M04-T12-FENCE-READY releases early Rules guards before04-T08/09 without depending on full04-T12 in B16; full task completion remains after its original prerequisites. Independent count-contract approval is required before source changes. All final operational and integration criteria remain in force.</p>
<p>04-T02 additionally includes an I-owned real Firestore RSS regression fixture <code>firebase_tests/firebase-emulators/editorial-rss.test.js</code>, discovered by the existing editorial emulator glob. Both-root historical raw/decoded aliases, collisions and first-import/retry side effects must be exercised against actual transactions, not only snapshot fakes. This is the fifth04-T02path; no new task/batch/wave/script or dependency is introduced.</p>
<h2 id="b13-demo-only-verified-interim-handoff">B13 demo-only verified interim handoff</h2>
<p>RSS identity/decoding implementation and guarded repair tooling passed independent re-review following three high-priority safeguard corrections. Permanent pre-fix regressions show four intended rejection failures; final40 guard tests and73 actual editorial emulator tests pass with zero skips. <code>B13-review.md</code> preserves both the original rejection and the subsequent independent approval with exact fingerprints. The permission fixture preserves existing administrative reservation reads, denies every client reservation write, and denies every client read/write/list of new repair jobs and receipts in both roots. No production operation occurred. B15 count-fence integration, full Work Order acceptance and the original unexplained transfer-test instability remain pending; R09 is OPEN.</p>
<h3 id="m04-t12-fence-ready-field-type-and-namespace-clarification">M04-T12-FENCE-READY field-type and namespace clarification</h3>
<p>The independently approved data contract specifies exact root-fence types, including native trusted-commit Timestamp <code>activeFrom</code> and <code>baselineManifestHash</code>. Use the unreleased private <code>contributions/{commentId}</code> leaf collection, avoiding existing administrator <code>/comments</code> collection-group list Rules. Preserve canonical comment queries and existing <code>importKeys</code> reads; no Rules change broadens access. Before any later authorized count maintenance, reconciliation, apply, restore or activation scope, perform a bounded read-only preflight of the old planned <code>/comments</code> ledger namespace and refuse mutation/activation if records exist. Normal event/writer transactions do not scan the entire ledger. No automatic rename, copy, delete or live migration is authorized. The initial old-path leak probe is a retained design mismatch; new-path default-deny checks are GREEN guards. The paused-root authorized-create assertion is the behavioral RED for this partial Rules milestone. Keep65tasks/16batches/17waves; full04-T12 and B15/B16 acceptance, all existing verification obligations and production approvals remain outstanding.</p>
<h3 id="b15-count-baseline-fixture-and-isolated-runner-refinement">B15 count-baseline fixture and isolated-runner refinement</h3>
<p>Accepted count activation requires legitimate native baselines before existing emulator journeys. Task04-T08 therefore includes the exact additional fixture/support paths registered in <code>waves.json</code>, as explicit compatibility attachments to the original task. QA supplies patches and I is the sole writer. New support is <code>firebase_tests/support/comment-count-fixtures.mjs</code> and <code>tool/run-count-emulator-tests.mjs</code>; existing fixture seeds are adapted only where required. Two package.json emulator script targets may route to the isolated runner while retaining command names; no dependency, lockfile, build or deployment configuration changes are authorized. Standalone and admin harnesses use real production authority/handler helpers, controlled demo bootstrap, no developer secrets/external senders, and serialized test files; dedicated concurrent transaction cases remain. No assertion is weakened and new-comment expected counts are never seeded after creation. Root-global bootstrap/maintenance is isolated, all original17 identities execute, and final acceptance remains pending. This necessary test-support expansion supersedes the original per-task five-file planning estimate without adding or renumbering the65 canonical task IDs or17 waves.</p>
<h3 id="b15-empty-demo-root-bootstrap-phase-without-a-dependency-cycle">B15 empty-demo-root bootstrap phase without a dependency cycle</h3>
<p>Real04-T08 worker tests require an accepted baseline before creating comments. The genuine bootstrap implementation belongs to04-T09, whose full reconciliation/restore acceptance follows04-T08. <code>M04-T09-BOOTSTRAP-READY</code> therefore records only the early guarded empty-demo-root tool/code preparation from04-T09 after04-T06,04-T07 and the approved early Rules guard.04-T08 consumes that partial artifact; full04-T09 still waits for04-T08. The partial phase never fabricates an active fence, seeds an expected post-comment count, authorizes production, or completes the producer task. The combined graph has87 acyclic task/milestone/checkpoint nodes with no unknown references; the65 task IDs,16 batches and17 waves are unchanged.</p>
